      "Abstract": {"AbstractText": [
        {
          "NlmCategory": "OBJECTIVE",
          "Label": "BACKGROUND AND RATIONALE",
          "content": "The authors report the quantitation of myocardial enhancement using iodinated contrast medium in patients with ischemic heart disease. Twenty-eight patients with chronic ischemic heart disease and 11 controls were examined by ultrafast computed tomography (CT) using 100-msecond scans."
        },
        {
          "NlmCategory": "METHODS",
          "Label": "METHODS",
          "content": "The authors analyzed M/L (ratio of post-contrast incremental increases in the left ventricular myocardial and luminal CT number) in early and late phases after contrast injection."
        },
        {
          "NlmCategory": "RESULTS",
          "Label": "RESULTS",
          "content": "In controls, mean values of early and late M/L were 30% and 51%, respectively. In infarcted or severely ischemic segments, early M/Ls (19%, 16%) were significantly small (P less than .001), whereas late M/Ls (90%, 63%) were higher (P less than .001, .01) than controls. Segments with infarction or severe ischemia were differentiated from mild or nonsignificant ischemia by using this parameter (sensitivity, 99%; specificity, 88%)."
        },
        {
          "NlmCategory": "CONCLUSIONS",
          "Label": "CONCLUSIONS",
          "content": "M/L is useful for detection of the ischemic myocardium."
        }
      ]},
